  "body": "The consumer code touching the ReadableStream API cannot obtain fine-grained control over how much data to pull. It's hidden. So, in case, big chunks are used by the data source, the consumer code may get unexpectedly big chunk from a read() call. It's ok to get a big chunk, but I don't want the ReadableStream to start pulling new data on that read() call as the consumer code is being overwhelmed by that big data chunk and it shouldn't be immediately considered to have been consumed.\n\nIn the W3C spec, I tried to address this by amountBeingReturned. Could you please investigate this issue?\n",
